    "description": {
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Source: https://metricell.atlassian.net/browse/VM2ST-231\nCopied from a Done VMO2 SmartTools subtask for TEST2 browser QA. The SmartTools issue remains unchanged."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Purpose: Provide the Surveyor-owned Display Settings control beneath the V4 GIS legend."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Acceptance criteria:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bulletList",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "listItem",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Presentation controls are available for a loaded Surveyor layer."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "listItem",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Changing presentation settings does not change the underlying filtered result set."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "listItem",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Display Settings appears beneath the Surveyor legend."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "listItem",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "The available controls include active legend/colouring, Show Linked Sites, Show Linked Cells when linked sites and the zoom gate allow it, Colour Point Links By Azimuth/Band only for the Band legend with linked sites shown, and Show Labels only for Building."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "listItem",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "No Sector control is exposed."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "listItem",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Options persist across normal GIS state restoration."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Validation: Load a Surveyor layer in V4 GIS, inspect the layer-owned Display Settings, exercise controls whose prerequisites are available, and check persistence. Distinguish unavailable data or permissions from failed UI behaviour; do not infer unchanged query results from screenshots alone. This depends on the Surveyor catalogue and layer fixture/adapter and may need suitable account access and data."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
